messages:
emily: heads up — CI/GitOps saw spurious diffs for gpu-nodepool config, manifests keep reordering. Not changing values, just ordering.
emily: failed in argo/CD after terraform apply, helm-diff showed map keys shuffled. Repro: ran `helm template` twice and diffed outputs.
raj: can you paste the template helper? suspect range over map without sort.
emily: here is helper:
```
{{- define "infra.nodepools" -}}
{{- range $name, $spec := .Values.nodepools }}
apiVersion: v1
kind: NodePool
metadata:
  name: {{ $name }}
spec:
  gpus: {{ $spec.gpu }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}
```
emily: Values is a map in values.yaml, so order is nondeterministic.
michael: yep. fix is to iterate sorted keys: use `keys` + `sortAlpha` + `index` e.g.
```
{{- $ks := sortAlpha (keys .Values.nodepools) -}}
{{- range $i, $k := $ks -}}
  {{- $spec := index .Values.nodepools $k -}}
  apiVersion: v1
  kind: NodePool
  metadata:
    name: {{ $k }}
  spec:
    gpus: {{ $spec.gpu }}
{{- end }}
```
raj: also add a small unit test in helm-chart-ci: render twice and assert outputs identical. We could add a helm-lint plugin rule to flag `range .* := .* .Values` patterns.
emily: opened PR with fix and test: https://git.redwood/infradeploy/helm-charts/pull/412
ops-bot: pipeline failed on old branch due to ordering; see build 8921 https://ci.redwood/build/8921 :warning:
michael: agreeing — we'll add a pre-merge check to run `helm template` twice in the chart-smoke test and diff. also log this in infra playbook.
emily: thanks all, rolling out fix to other charts now :thumbsup:
